[? if year == 2021 and month == 1 and democrat_president == 1: As congress considers a second impeachment of the disgraced former president Donald Trump, Trump seems set on attempting a political comback. Reports have leaked that the President, frustrated with the reluctance many in the <span style="color: #DE0100;">**Republican party**</span> have shown towards defending him, is seriously considering the formation of a third party, deemed the "<span style="color: #A356DE ;">Patriot Party</span>." The media has reported that a new PAC called the Patriot Party PAC was recently registered, and Trump has reportedly been calling up former allies in the <span style="color: #DE0100;">Republican party</span> to try and guage support. It is unclear if the President is serious, or if he is bluffing to try and pressure <span style="color: #DE0100;">Republicans</span> into supporting him in his upcoming impeachment trial. As a result of vote splitting, if Trump truly formed his own party, it would almost gurantee <span style="color: #3E88B3;">democratic</span> wins in competitive states. In response, <span style="color: #DE0100;">**Republicans**</span> such as minority speaker Kevin Mccarthy, who were talking about throwing Trump overseas just a few weeks ago, seem to be walking back their rhetoric. There are even reports that Mccarthy is preparing to meet Trump at Maralago in the coming weeks, at the great annoyance of moderate <span style="color: #DE0100;">**Republican**</span> house members who see the former President as nothing but a burden on the party. ?]

[? if year == 2021 and month == 1 and democrat_president == 1: In the primary for Virginia governor, blah blah blah blah. ?]

